A||N||4||MISTER_PORKY||SPEEDOMETER SENDING UNTI GEAR||||9||
Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-02-2001||06:25 PM||||<BR>I HAVE AN '84 FIERO WITH A 4 SPEED MANUAL TRANNY. LAST WEEK I WENT TO CHANGE THE OIL IN THE GEAR BOX, AND THE GEAR ON THE SPEEDOMETER SENDING UNIT SHAFT FELL DOWN INTO THE GEAR BOX. ANY IDES ON HOW TO RETRIEVE IT SHORT OF PULLING THE ENGINE CRADLE OR AN AXLE SHAFT ? <BR>    THIS IS, BY THE WAY, A ONE OWNER CAR, MEANING I BOUGHT IT NEW BACK IN '84, AND HAS OVER 100K VITRUALY TROUBLE FREE MILES ON IT ! <BR>    THANKS FOR ANY IDEAS !||||reg||9
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||09-02-2001||08:05 PM||||Gosh I dont think that this has happened to anybody while I Have been on the forum Lets see I think the gear is plastic so a magnet wont help. I guess that I would try taking a piece of tie wire and make a hook on the end and try to fish it out that way.I dont have any other ideas.I know that I would work with that wire idea a long time before I would even consider yanking the tranny .||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||09-02-2001||08:38 PM||||Correct me if I,m wrong but I believe that the lost gear is unlikly to cause any damage even if it manages to get in the other gears. It is plastic! Just get another gear if you can't fish it out. <BR>Getting the gear out on the shaft is tricky, Kind of like defusing a bomb. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-02-2001||09:29 PM||||The gear is not likely to cause any damage, but it may prevent the trans from working properly. V8Dreamer checked his trans oil and his speedometer stopped working at the same time. He never even knew the gear was there. Well about a week later he couldn't get it into first or reverse at all. Little bits of plastic had worked their way up into the shift linkage area at the top of the trans and jammed everything up. His was an Isuzu 5 speed which has the removeable cover on top so we were able to pull it apart and get a lot of it out. We were prepared to replace the trans, even picked up another one, but it has been working fine. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||85Josh||09-03-2001||02:49 PM||||rockcrawl is right. I lost my gear into my Isuzu 5-speed, and it jammed my shifter about a week later. I just recently had the tranny out to change the clutch, and found dozens of tiny bits of gear in the oil. No other damage, though.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
